cff-version: 1.2.0

# ── Project identity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title: "Permi"

abstract: >
  Permi is an open-source security signal filter for African fintech
  engineering teams. It scans source code and live web applications for
  security vulnerabilities — including SQL injection, cross-site scripting,
  hardcoded secrets, and insecure practices — then uses an AI filter to remove
  false positives so developers only see findings that actually matter.
  Permi includes rules built specifically for the Nigerian development context:
  USSD gateway misconfigurations, Paystack and Flutterwave credential exposure,
  and patterns relevant to Nigeria Data Protection Act (NDPA) compliance.
  It runs entirely locally with no mandatory cloud backend, storing results in
  a local SQLite database. Permi is distributed as a Python CLI package via
  PyPI and as a GitHub Action on the GitHub Marketplace. It is designed to be
  the default security workflow tool for African fintech engineering teams —
  the layer between a developer's code editor and their regulatory obligations
  that no foreign tool currently occupies.

